CASE = [
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> Every year, lakhs of warkaris walk for about two weeks from villages across Maharashtra, singing devotional songs, to reach Pandharpur. Strangers share food and shelter along the way. "
   "(i) What is this pilgrimage called? (ii) At which town does it end? (iii) In which state is that town? (iv) Why do pilgrimages like this help to bring people together?",
   "(i) The Wari (1). (ii) Pandharpur (1). (iii) Maharashtra (1). (iv) People of different backgrounds travel and sing together (1); sharing food and effort builds a sense of unity and shared belief (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> Beside a village in Meghalaya stands a dense patch of forest that nobody is allowed to cut. Villagers say a deity lives there, and even dead wood is not taken. Scientists find that rare plants and birds survive in the patch. "
   "(i) What is such a forest called? (ii) Why do villagers protect it? (iii) Name one benefit of such a forest. (iv) How can religious belief help to protect the environment?",
   "(i) A sacred grove (1). (ii) They believe it is the abode of a deity (1). (iii) It preserves plants, birds or water sources (1). (iv) Belief makes people care for nature and avoid damage (1); traditions passed on over generations protect biodiversity without laws (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> The Dongria Kondh of Odisha regard Niyam Dongar as sacred and the abode of their deity. Far away, the Maori people of New Zealand regard Taranaki Maunga as an ancestor. Both communities hold their mountains in deep respect. "
   "(i) Which community in Odisha holds Niyam Dongar sacred? (ii) Which mountain is an ancestor for the Maori? (iii) In which country do the Maori live? (iv) What does the passage show about how people in different parts of the world view nature?",
   "(i) The Dongria Kondh (1). (ii) Taranaki Maunga (1). (iii) New Zealand (1). (iv) Many communities see mountains and nature as sacred (1); this reverence leads them to protect these places (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
]

